photoc helps you review, organize, and prepare photos from the
terminal: summarize a shoot, read metadata, find blurry shots and
exact duplicates, rename and sort into folders, make contact sheets
and smaller copies, or remove GPS before sharing. Most commands
work in shell scripts; `review` needs a terminal. Inspection commands
can print JSON. Large JPEGs may use temporary in-memory previews,
which do not change the originals. photoc reads JPEG files and
metadata from Sony ARW RAW files as of now.
